5. Definition of Done
A task is considered Done when:

Code runs without errors
Markdown explanation is present (for analysis/visualization tasks)
Changes are committed to Git with a clear message
Partner has had a chance to review (or pair-programmed)
The entire project is Done when:

All cells in the notebook execute successfully from top to bottom
≥ 3 visualizations are properly labeled
≥ 3 business insights are clearly stated
Final conclusions section is complete
README is up to date
Repository is pushed to GitHub
6. Project Risks & Mitigations
#	Risk	Likelihood	Impact	Mitigation Action
1	Poor data quality or limited dataset size affects accuracy of conclusions	Medium	High	Perform thorough data cleaning and validation early (T2–T4). Document any limitations clearly in the notebook.
2	Delays in collaboration or uneven task ownership impact the deadline	Medium	High	Use this Kanban board daily. Hold short 10-minute check-ins. Clearly assign owners and update status frequently.
